# Gravelgill Scoundrel: "Whenever this creature attacks, you may tap another untapped creature you control. If you do, this creature can't be blocked
# this turn" (CR 701.26a, 509.1b). On turn 3 the two Ornithopters (not Bot2's Elvish Mystic, not the Scoundrel itself) are what the trigger offers, and
# only one may be tapped; tapping it, Bot2's Mystic may not block the Scoundrel, which has vigilance. On turn 5 Bot1 answers none, the Scoundrel is
# blockable again and the Mystic blocks it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Gravelgill Scoundrel
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Elvish Mystic
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Gravelgill Scoundrel.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Gravelgill Scoundrel > Bot2)
! Bot1.Choose(Gravelgill Scoundrel)
! Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter#1; Ornithopter#2)
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter#1)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
! Bot2.Block
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Tapped = True
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Tapped = False
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Gravelgill Scoundrel > Bot2)
Bot1.Choose()
[T5 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
Bot2.Block(Elvish Mystic > Gravelgill Scoundrel)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Tapped = False
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Tapped = False
